                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "96de7194-5221-3123-89cc-3b27f7f78696",
                        "entry_id": "e791c839-8d3d-3640-bd35-c4b42e94eec4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To match more than intended."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "abfd27b4-27a1-408f-9cfc-46d6a5cb49f8",
                                "sense_id": "96de7194-5221-3123-89cc-3b27f7f78696",
                                "text": "The regular expression overmatched, capturing the entire paragraph instead of the specific sentence."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7c98f710-2229-3963-b463-c4de9319e4aa",
                        "entry_id": "e791c839-8d3d-3640-bd35-c4b42e94eec4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To be more than equal to or a match for, to surpass; hence, to conquer, vanquish."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "838b1e65-0690-42eb-9b26-8d0262570f62",
                                "sense_id": "7c98f710-2229-3963-b463-c4de9319e4aa",
                                "text": "And wel his merits ſhew him to be made\nHis Fortunes maiſter, and the king of men.\nThat could perſwade at ſuch a ſodaine pinch,\nWith reaſons of his valour and his life,\nA thouſand ſworne and ouer-matching foes:"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "31de8644-9e73-4d8a-8a22-2d4f154a8a22",
                                "sense_id": "7c98f710-2229-3963-b463-c4de9319e4aa",
                                "text": "At Lemster, for her Wooll whose Staple doth excell,\nAnd seemes to over-match the golden Phrygian Fell."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7acde628-0b1c-3fdd-aad4-d273a07263e5",
                        "entry_id": "e791c839-8d3d-3640-bd35-c4b42e94eec4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To marry (someone) to a superior."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea15bae4-4640-43e1-81f7-7725b08657ea",
                                "sense_id": "7acde628-0b1c-3fdd-aad4-d273a07263e5",
                                "text": "If a yeoman have one sole daughter, he must overmatch her, above her birth and calling, to a gentleman forsooth, because of her great portion […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
